x86/mm/pat: skip RWX verification until kernel text is set to read only

A 7.3.x stable update (038176c21617, effective RW computation in
lookup_address_in_pgd_attr) made verify_rwx() see the temporary RWX pages of
the ITS thunks that apply_retpolines() allocates during early boot, and the
kernel warned once and tainted itself (W) on every affected Intel CPU.
This is the fix Mike Rapoport posted upstream (LKML, 2026-09); it is carried
here until a stable release has it.

--- a/arch/x86/mm/pat/set_memory.c
+++ b/arch/x86/mm/pat/set_memory.c
@@ -708,6 +708,15 @@
 	if (!(__supported_pte_mask & _PAGE_NX))
 		return new;
 
+	/*
+	 * Skip verification until kernel text is set to read only: until
+	 * then all of kernel text is mapped RWX for alternatives patching,
+	 * and the temporary RWX pages of the ITS thunks are expected.
+	 * CONFIG_DEBUG_WX still checks every mapping once it is.
+	 */
+	if (!kernel_set_to_readonly)
+		return new;
+
 	if (!((pgprot_val(old) ^ pgprot_val(new)) & (_PAGE_RW | _PAGE_NX)))
 		return new;
 
